CLASS & OBJECT-=====>

1->
Class- Class is template or blueprint of objects. User define datatypes that has data member and member function. Used to create objects.
Object- Object is an instance of classes.
Example:
- world is class and india(exist in world) is object.
- india is class and up(exist in india) is object.
- up is class and sonbhadra(exist in up) is object.

2->
Defining class and object.
Syntax:
//class
Class Classname
{
    Access specifier:  [can be public,private, or protected]
    Data memeber;  [variable to be used]
    Member function()  [method to access data member]
    {
        Statement;
    }
};  [class name end with semicolon]
//object
Classname Objectname;
Objectname.data member;
Objectname.member function;

3->
Scope resolution operator [ :: ]-
- The scope resolution operator allows you to access variables, functions, or classes within a specific namespace. Accessing Global Variables: When you have a local variable with the same name as a global variable, the scope resolution operator lets you access the global variable from within a function or block.
- Used to aceess method from outside the class.

